Here are 5 specific, actionable recommendations for the gate "Set circuit breakers on outgoing requests":

1. Implement a global circuit breaker in the Spring Boot application configuration file (e.g., `application.properties` or `application.yml`) to set a timeout and reset mechanism for outgoing requests. This will ensure that if any downstream service is unresponsive, the entire request chain can be retried after a certain period of time.

Specifically, add the following configuration properties:
```properties
spring:
  circuitbreaker:
    enabled: true
    retry:
      maxAttempts: 3
      timeout: 5000ms
```
This will enable circuit breaking for all outgoing requests and set a maximum number of retries to 3 with a timeout of 5 seconds.

2. Review the `RestTemplate` configuration in the `application.properties` file (or equivalent) to ensure that it is properly configured to use a circuit breaker. If not, add the following configuration:
```properties
spring:
  web:
    resttemplate:
      enabled: true
      circuitbreaker:
        enabled: true
```
This will enable circuit breaking for all `RestTemplate` requests.

3. Identify and refactor any existing code that uses synchronous blocking calls to downstream services. Instead, use asynchronous callbacks or promises to allow the circuit breaker to detect unresponsive services and trigger retries. For example, in a Java method that makes an HTTP request using `RestTemplate`, replace the synchronous call with an asynchronous one:
```java
@RestController
public class MyController {
    @Autowired
    private RestTemplate restTemplate;

    @GetMapping("/my-endpoint")
    public String myEndpoint() {
        return restTemplate.getForObject("https://downstream-service.com/my-endpoint", String.class);
    }

    // Refactored version using asynchronous callbacks:
    @GetMapping("/my-endpoint")
    public Future<String> myEndpointAsync() {
        Callable<String> callable = () -> restTemplate.getForObject("https://downstream-service.com/my-endpoint", String.class);
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(callable, executorService());
    }
}
```
This refactoring will allow the circuit breaker to detect unresponsive services and trigger retries.

